5. Governing Equations (Conceptual Form)

5.1 Gravitational Energy Field

[ E = \int_V G(r, t), dV ]

Where ( G(r, t) ) is derived from astrophysical datasets and acts as a forcing term in geomechanical and fluid equations.

5.2 Geomechanics — Biot Consolidation

[ \partial_t\left(\frac{p_M}{M} + \alpha \nabla\cdot \mathbf{u}\right) = \nabla\cdot\left(\frac{k}{\mu}\nabla p\right) + Q' ]

( p_M ): matrix pressure

( M ): constrained modulus

( \alpha ): Biot coefficient

( \mathbf{u} ): displacement field

( k ): permeability

( \mu ): fluid viscosity

( Q' ): source/sink term

5.3 Multiphase Flow (Water–Methane)

[ \mathbf{v}i = -\frac{k k{ri}}{\mu_i} \nabla p_i ]

[ S_w + S_g = 1 ]

( \mathbf{v}_i ): phase velocity

( k_{ri} ): relative permeability

( \mu_i ): phase viscosity

( S_w, S_g ): water and gas saturations

5.4 Fracture Mechanics — Mohr‑Coulomb Yield

[ \sigma_{\text{yield}} = C + \sigma_n \tan(\phi) ]

Failure occurs when shear stress ( \tau \ge \sigma_{\text{yield}} ).

5.5 Biogeochemical Reaction‑Diffusion

[ \partial_t C_i = D_i \nabla^2 C_i + R_i(C_i, T, P, S) ]

( C_i ): concentration of species ( i )

( D_i ): diffusion coefficient

( R_i ): nonlinear reaction term (microbial, chemical)

( T, P, S ): temperature, pressure, salinity

5.6 Unified State Vector

[ \Psi = {u, p, S_i, C_i, \sigma, \tau, T, P, S} ]

All modules read from and write to ( \Psi ), ensuring full coupling.

